      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'The law sets no overall timetable, and it varies by emirate and by how quickly the husband can be served. Article 79 of Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2024 builds in fixed waits: if his address is known, he is warned and given up to 180 days; if he is missing, no divorce can be granted until one year after filing. In practice these cases usually take several months and can take more than a year. A divorce for non-payment under Article 77 is usually quicker, since his grace period is at most 30 days (90 if he proves he cannot pay). Non-Muslim civil divorce is usually quickest, because the court can rule at the first hearing once he has been served.',
